// Command loadtest drives this project's player TCP listener with robots.
//
//	go run ./cmd/accountctl upsert-server -sid 1000        # once: account must know the server
//	go run ./cmd/loadtest -endpoint 127.0.0.1:7000 -count 20 -account-nats nats://127.0.0.1:4222
//	go run ./cmd/loadtest -login portal -portal http://127.0.0.1:8081 -count 20   # log in the way a client does
//
// Two ways to log in (-login). The default, bus, is the one a login server
// takes: Login → CreateRole → SelectRole on the account service over the bus,
// then a session ticket on the handshake. portal is the client's way through
// the front door (the portal module, HTTP on the account process): login →
// server list → enter ticket, handshake with enter:<ticket>, wait for the
// server's EnterStatus, send EnterCreate when it says so, then EnterGame.
//
// It is a load test and the demo's regression test in one: every robot logs
// in through the account service, creates or loads its Player, adds an item,
// levels up, queues for a duel until the matchmaker pairs it, reads the
// World's counters, and the run fails on any non-zero response code or on a
// threshold breach. Use an even -count: duels need pairs. The runner, scenario tree, action registry and threshold
// gate are roost-core/robot; this file only registers the project's messages
// and the transport that speaks the generated server's frame.
